 "device_note": "cuda:0 was at 100% utilization (other agents' C4 TRIM jobs and an unrelated user's processes), so every Phase M GPU job ran on cuda:1, which was idle (0%, 70 MiB) before each launch. scaling_v5_002 ran alone. The formal rows and probes ran as 9 concurrent processes, so their wall_s values are contended and are not timing evidence.",
 "seeds": "seed 42 (run_phase1_matrix SEED, kinematic reset); blade_probe probes are deterministic plans without a seed",
 "resolution": "particle spacing 1 mm, grid dx 4 mm, material dt 1e-4 s, control dt 0.02 s, cutting law 8, ruler_knife_v1 edge",
 "design": {
  "packed_digits": "int32 code, d_k = (code >> 2k) & 3, 0 unassigned / 1 negative / 2 positive / 3 invalid, K <= 15. Assignment only from d_k = 0: code |= d << 2k. The kernel guards cut < K, and set_trajectory rejects cut >= K. Conflict: A1 = L & ~H and A2 = H & ~L with L = code & 0x5555..., H = (code >> 1) & 0x5555...; codes conflict iff (A1a & A2b) | (A2a & A1b) != 0.",
  "slot_claim": "Every substep slot_code (N*S, -1 = empty) is filled with -1. Then _claim_slots runs over (particle, corner): it walks slots 0..S-1 of the node, reads a slot and CASes it from -1 to its code when empty, and takes the first slot holding its own code. Slots therefore fill as a contiguous prefix of distinct codes, and slot[p, corner] stores the slot index. P2G, G2P, MUSL and the F update address node*S + slot.",
  "grid_update": "Launch (S, N). An occupied slot with m > 1e-15 sums total mass and the pairwise antisymmetric exchange over the other occupied slots, visiting them in ascending code order (selection over <= S slots). That is v4's field order, because ternary and packed codes order digits identically, and the exchange is v4's (m*(p_j+j_j) - m_j*raw)/M_total over compatible fields. O(S^2) work per node, independent of K.",
  "overflow": "More than S distinct codes at a node: the entry gets slot -1, is skipped in P2G/G2P/MUSL/F (never merged), and is counted atomically in slot_overflow (cumulative). The host raises SlotOverflowError after every control step (LiveCuttingMaterial.advance) and after every blade_probe chunk. slot_max_occupied (cumulative atomic max) is the diagnostic.",
  "determinism": "CPU: v5 equals v4 bit for bit for K <= 2 on every law-8 CPU scenario tested (tests/test_tlmpm_v5.py). Accumulation order per field is identical and the grid update uses v4's field order. GPU: the slot index of a code is race dependent, but no floating-point sum depends on slot order. v5 therefore has v4's atomic-accumulation nondeterminism and no more: final codes match exactly, and positions differ within the v4 repeat-to-repeat spread (see v5_vs_v4_comparisons).",
  "cuda_graph": "step() is capturable (slot_code.fill_, the claim kernel and the fixed launch dims). LiveCuttingMaterial captures it at reset and blade_probe gpu_graph captures it per chunk; both were exercised on cuda:1."
 },
