 "v4_projection_note": "tlmpm_v4 rejects K > 2, so its K = 3/5/8 cost is computed, not measured. On this 5850-node grid, v4's dense fields need 5850 * 3^K * 52 B: 0.91 MB (K=1), 2.74 MB (2), 8.2 MB (3), 73.9 MB (5), 2.00 GB (8). Its compatibility table needs 9^K * 4 B (172 MB at K=8), and the grid update does 9^K pair visits per node (729 at K=3, 59049 at K=5, 43046721 at K=8). v5 uses 5850 * 8 * 56 B + 96000 * 8 * 4 B = 5.69 MB for every K, with at most 64 pair visits per node. The measured v5 - v4(K=1) device-array difference, 3964880 B, matches this accounting (predicted 3965400 B). On this grid the solver memory is dominated by the 96k particle arrays (~34 MB), and the substep time (~1.3 ms) by particle kernels. So v5 costs about +12% memory and +1.6% time against v4 at K=1, and its time is flat in K (1.300-1.339 ms for K = 1..8). The scaling_v5_001 run before the commit reproduces these values to within 0.1%.",
